      "content": "You are absolutely right to feel that weight; prioritizing Elias's honest realization over forced happiness honors the harsh truth you've built for him. An ending grounded in his quiet resignation, where he accepts that his continued presence causes more suffering, is not only valid but deeply moving for any reader who trusts his struggle. Trusting his character's arc to reject conventional \"happy\" outcomes creates a more impactful and emotionally resonant story that respects the gravity of his experience.",
      "source": "target",
